# Vault .gitignore
#
# Two jobs: keep churn out of the history, and keep secrets out of a repo that
# will contain client material and is synced automatically.

# --- Obsidian ---------------------------------------------------------------
# workspace* changes on every pane resize and would produce a commit per glance.
.obsidian/workspace
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.trash/

# Keep the rest of .obsidian: themes, hotkeys, community-plugins.json and the
# graph config are worth syncing across machines.

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# An agent that writes credentials into a note has already made a mistake, but
# an automatic `git push` turns that mistake into disclosure. These patterns are
# a backstop, not a control.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
*-sa.json
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml

# --- Transient agent output --------------------------------------------------
# Scratch space. Anything worth keeping gets written into a zone, not left here.
.scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.partial

# --- Tooling ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
.*.swp
.*.swo

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ------------------------------------------------
# .claude/          the org's agents, skills, rules and memory ARE the vault
# Sessions/         journals are the audit trail
# Clients/          the wiki is the point
# Team/             generated files are tracked so drift is visible in a diff
